WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
Picture a small town where a
new engineering college opens.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.510
Four years later, its first graduates
are looking for work nearby.

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.730
The town now has far more
engineers willing to work,

4
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.420
at every wage.

5
00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.110
So what makes people willing to do a job,

6
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.810
and why isn't the pay the whole story?

7
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.490
In this mission, you'll
see why the labor supply

8
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.480
curve slopes upward as the wage rises.

9
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.890
Then you'll find the forces
that shift the whole curve,

10
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.160
from immigration to culture.

11
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.340
Your mission: find out what
really decides how much

12
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.320
labor people are willing to supply.
